### Do not log expected supersession cancellation as a render failure

**Severity:** `medium`

Once superseded pending updates are canceled, rapid card refreshes can naturally cancel an older `DisplayCardAsync` call. Handling `OperationCanceledException` before the general error path avoids logging expected latest-wins behavior as an Adaptive Card update failure.

```suggestion
            await _cardUpdater.UpdateAsync(card);
            AttachRenderedCard(_cardUpdater.RenderedCard);
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException)
        {
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            Logger.LogError("Failed to update an Adaptive Card", ex);
```
